WEBVTT

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.400
The Diva has reached Earth's escape velocity.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.490
Setting a course for Luna base.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.280
No sign of enemies in the area.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.450
Well, I guess we've passed the first hurdle.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.410
Now we can relax a little.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.580
It looks like the diversion worked.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.920
Now that the pressure's off, I'm getting hungry.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.920
That's all you ever talk about, isn't it?{You really can't talk about anything else, can you?}

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.430
E-Everyone! Please remain on high alert!

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.600
Captain.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:39.930
Yes!

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.850
You can take your helmet off now.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.350
Huh?

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.900
Hey! Come on, Kio!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.820
Kio? Something wrong?

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.190
Someone... is waiting for us.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.330
So you're here, Diva.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.380
The Mars settlement plan.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.930
The people left behind in the Mars Sphere in the wake of its failure

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.850
formed the independent nation of Vagan,

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.560
and launched a war against the Earth Federation government.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.360
70 years have already passed

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:16.320
since the conflict began.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.950
todokasete kono mune ni

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.950
Let your voice reach my heart

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.460
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.460
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.880
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.880
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.630
samayoitsuzuketeita

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.630
I kept wandering

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.390
tachidomaru no mo mae ni susumu koto mo

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.390
Halting in your tracks and walking ahead proudly

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.850
atozusari na ki ga shiteta

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.850
both seemed too fearsome a choice

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.320
tojikomerareta shikakui sora no shita

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.320
Here on the board, where we are bound to

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.570
iki wo hisometeta

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.570
I tried to breathe softly to blend in

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:05.990
tsumetai hoho wo tsutawaru kako no yowasa nugutte

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:05.990
I swept away the weakness of the past trailing down my cheeks

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:12.460
hikari sasu basho he kono te wo nobasu yo

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:12.460
and held out my hands to the light

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.050
todokasete kono mune ni

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.050
Let your voice reach my heart

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.550
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.550
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.970
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.970
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.930
sagashitsuzuketeru

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.930
I kept searching

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.060
todokaseru sono mune ni

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.060
I will let my feelings and my voice

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.480
tashika na omoi boku no koe wo

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.480
reach your heart

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.900
owaranai genjitsu de

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.900
Through days without end

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.320
sakebitsuzuketeiku

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.320
I will be proud, be strong

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:48.160
ashita wo shinjite

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:48.160
and have faith in the future

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:55.840
Episode 34 
Space Pirates 
Bisidian

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.090
The Diva's whereabouts remain unknown.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:04.260
Our informants on Earth say it left Rostroulan carrying the Gundam.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.550
I am already putting a plan in motion.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.560
Please leave it to me.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.400
Now that you're working for me, 
you'd better prove yourself useful.{lol comma splice}{he's asking for *special* favours}

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.820
I definitely won't disappoint you, Master Zeheart.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.410
<i>Zeheart Galette...</i>

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:34.000
<i>My brother gave his life for you.</i>

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.090
<i>If you're not worthy of that, I'll kill you myself.</i>

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.180
What do we do next?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.020
Zero-gravity hide and seek!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.390
Okay!

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.350
Hey.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.850
Wootbit.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.190
They seem lively.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.520
Everybody's excited now that we're in space.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.690
You're such little kids.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.070
You were excited too!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.780
We saw you!

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.200
You're acting like little kid, too.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.790
Little kid! Little kid!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.050
Anyway, how long are you guys staying on this ship?

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:25.970
We found out all their families were 
evacuated to a colony near the moon.{the capitalization of the word "moon" is apparently debatable}

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:33.390
Apparently the Federation Forces sent 
some of the people from Olivernotes there.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.850
So we're taking these kids to the Luna base.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.310
The military will send them on from there.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.610
I see.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.730
Kio?

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.320
We're gonna see our moms and dads soon!

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.650
That's good.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.820
Kio? Is something wrong?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.740
I just felt something...

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:56.620
As if someone was waiting in our path.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.620
That's kinda ominous.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.590
I just hope nothing happens before we get to the moon.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.010
Still detecting no immediate threats in the surrounding area.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.680
It seems the Vagan fleet fell for the decoy.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.930
What a relief...

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:16.020
But will we be okay? Up ahead is...

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.140
The special alert sector, right?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.150
Is there something there?{He was hoping for an all you can eat buffet}

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.730
You don't know?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.110
The special alert sector.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.700
It's known as... Sargasso.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.110
Sargasso?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:33.280
Yeah. It looks like we're about to pass through that sector.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.250
If somebody's waiting for us like you said,

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.830
they might be in there.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.250
What kind of place is it?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:43.210
It's a ghastly{evil spirts} place, full of drifting shipwrecks.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:49.680
There are lots of rumors about ships going in and not coming out, and instruments malfunctioning.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.850
Well, rumors are just rumors.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.640
Do we really have to go through there?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.520
The fact that ships do not normally travel there

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.270
means the Vagan are less likely to find us.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.020
Steady as she goes.{We're going in.}

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.150
Roger.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.910
It's kind of creepy.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.170
What looks like fog is actually droplets of ice.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.380
This says it's a comet swarm captured by a Lagrange point

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.550
that's gradually melting in the sun's heat.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.100
What?!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.760
Signal on enemy detection systems!

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:37.890
Identity unknown!

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.100
Size is battleship-class!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.270
Vagan?!

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.140
That's...

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.410
I've got you now, Diva!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.080
It doesn't match any Vagan ship in our database!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.590
Then what...?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.260
<i>Listen, Diva!</i>

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.510
<i>We are the Bisidian space pirates!</i>

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.550
<i>We're taking your ship!</i>

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.980
If you value your lives, surrender your ship peacefully!

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:27.150
<i>Otherwise, we'll seize it by force in the name of Bisidian!</i>

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:32.860
I can't believe we'd run into them here. Or is this an ambush?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.280
Grandpa, do you know them?

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:39.990
The Bisidian are pirates who've repeatedly attacked and plundered Federation ships.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.330
In other words, enemies of the Federation!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.210
So what do we do?

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.550
Prepare for anti-ship combat!

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.760
Abis team, please launch immediately!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.850
Kio!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.510
Right!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:08.440
Captain Ash, what's the point of attacking such an old ship?

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.150
Don't underestimate it.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.280
It carries an evolving monster.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:14.780
Captain?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.910
They'll never abandon that ship.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.330
I'm going out.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.370
I've never fought in space before.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.960
<i>If you can gather data in this battle,</i>

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.340
<i>the AGE System can produce some new wear parts.</i>

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.470
Right.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.590
<i>There's no need to be nervous.{Don't worry about it.}</i>

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.680
<i>Just trust in your previous experience, and fight.</i>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.350
<i>Fight to protect everyone.</i>

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.390
Right!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.340
Let's go, Abis team!{fuck yeah, extended launch sequence}

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:13.920
Launch!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.100
Kio Asuno, AGE-3. Here I go!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.620
Be careful! They're coming!

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:50.290
<i>Four mobile suits confirmed!</i>

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.880
There's one more coming!

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.210
Who are you?

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.980
We meet at last{We've finally met}, Kio.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:12.400
Show your father what you can do!{why pirate}

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.280
Let's go, Kio!{I mean, I saw that coming from a mile away}

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.020
I won't let you lay a hand{or other appropriate idiom} on the Diva!{Why else wouldn't they show his face}

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:00.610
Over here!{and he knows a lot about the diva and its crew, etc.}

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.830
Is that all you've got?{but I'm just not sure why he became a space pirate}

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.750
<i>Kio! Don't let your guard down!</i>

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:21.170
<i>The pilot of that mobile suit is probably Bisidian's leader!</i>

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.510
<i>He's a master pilot who's attacked many Federation ships!</i>

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.350
We have to defeat the Vagan!

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:35.980
We can't lose to <i>pirates</i>!

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.680
<i>Bisidian's leader...</i>

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:10.180
<i>I've heard no one knows his true identity.</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:15.810
<i>That suit looks like the AGE-2. But who in the world...?</i>

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.360
<i>I-Impossible!</i>

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:26.660
<i>This feeling... It can't be!</i>

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.990
<i>Is that you, Asemu?!</i>

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:40.590
<i>Father, I know you're aboard the Diva.</i>

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:45.010
<i>But now that you've left the military, just how much can you do?</i>

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:50.430
<i>I'll see if you're still worthy to use the AGE System!</i>

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.690
<i>And Kio, I'll test your power too!</i>

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:11.990
Derek, fall back!{check name}

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.330
All units, stay on guard!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.420
<i>Something's strange about this battle.</i>

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:26.340
<i>Even when they have the chance to deal a decisive blow, they don't.</i>

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.380
<i>It's like they're testing our strength.</i>

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.850
<i>Attention, Abis team! This is an emergency message!</i>

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.810
<i>I repeat, this is an emergency message!</i>

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:37.310
<i>Enemy detection systems have picked up what appear to be Vagan mobile suits!</i>

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.310
<i>Seven of them!</i>

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.770
<i>Approaching rapidly!</i>

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:41.190
{At a time like this}Why now, of all times?!{oh lord}

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.990
{That woman's searching abilities}{sounds so fag}Her scouting skills are impressive, I'll give her that!{is he wearing a suit?}{pirates don't need space suits...ask cpt ash}

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.200
Now it's hunting time!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.700
We'll take down the white one, no matter what!

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.910
This is for Deymon!

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:58.620
Right!

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.840
We've got to fight the Vagan too?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.380
This is bad! It's making me hungry!

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.300
Captain, what do we do?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.220
Captain, prepare to fire.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:21.770
Fire successively at sectors Bow 109 to 226, and 332 to 459!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:22.650
But why?

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.940
That won't hit them!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:25.570
It doesn't matter!{I LIKE WASTING AMMO. PROBLEM?}

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.660
Where are you shooting?!

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.500
So that's it...

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.460
Not bad, Father.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.630
Impressive.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:50.090
Avoiding those shots drove the 
Vagan between us and the Bisidian!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:55.050
So now the Diva pilots won't have to fight us!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.360
All that matters is taking out the white one!

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:07.940
Let's go!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.270
Wh-Where are they...?

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:44.190
I'm gonna tear you apart!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.780
<i>Kio... is that all you've got?</i>

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.510
That's right. That's what I want to see.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.100
C-Crap!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:25.440
Hope you're watching from the {next world}the other side, Deymon!{He's watching us all...from the next dimension!}

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:27.730
Get him!

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.360
No, you don't!

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.780
Take that!

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.420
Don't {mess with}underestimate a super pilot!{super pirate}

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:59.510
Deymon... I couldn't even...{I really hope deymon was watching}

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.360
Glatt!

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:18.490
Why?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.910
<i>Why did you save me?</i>

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:25.540
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.460
You're supposed be a dangerous enemy...

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.040
but I feel a warmth from you.{that's him raping you}

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:32.460
Why?

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.730
<i>I've seen your power.{and your spirit ball}</i>

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:56.070
<i>We'll meet again, Kio.</i>

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.990
The Bisidan and Vagan are both withdrawing from the area.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.280
<i>Asemu...</i>

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.000
<i>What are you trying to do?{I SEE YOUR MOUSE, REM}{my bad}</i>

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.420
<i>I'm very sorry. We've lost valuable soldiers.</i>

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.130
Never mind.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:21.050
That's not why I sent you to Zeheart.{yes it is...it's because he did the same damn thing}

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:24.430
I sent you to observe him.{homo? voyuer?}

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.140
I understand, Master Zanald.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:32.060
<i>Like myself, Zeheart works directly under Lord Ezelcant.</i>

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:36.730
<i>We cannot overlook the slightest error or change of heart.</i>

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:39.150
<i>Don't forget that.</i>

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:39.990
Yes, sir!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.280
What I'm after {something else}is different, though.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:55.590
Master Zeheart, I deeply apologize for the failure of the operation.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.300
I will devote myself to becoming a better commander,

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.590
so as not to embarrass the Zeheart team—

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.640
Do you know the names of the 
soldiers who died in this operation?

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.050
No...

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.350
Sam Kalev.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.350
Lin Foster.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.480
And Glatt Otto.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.520
They had fierce tempers, but they were skilled pilots.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.360
Remember them.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:17.940
Yes, sir!

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.740
Kio, I'm glad you're okay!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.210
You did good too, AGE-3.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.050
What's this?

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.640
Grandpa...

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.020
That pirate leader saved me.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.730
Did you feel {something}anything?

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:59.440
Yes. I've felt it over and over again since we got here.{That's lots of rape man}

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.690
Did you feel it too?

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.530
You know who that person was, don't you?

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.120
Yes.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.950
You're an X-Rounder, {I can't hide it from you}so there's no hiding it from you.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:18.460
The pilot of that mobile suit was Asemu Asuno. Your father.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.050
Captain Ash...

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.470
I know what you're going to say.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.890
Why did we withdraw before we got the Diva, right?

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:36.520
Our target was the AGE System aboard the Diva.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:41.780
Until now, we've attacked Federation units who were working with Vagan,

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.820
in order to reform the Federation.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:47.990
But we'll never make much progress that way.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:50.410
So you wanted the AGE System...

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.660
Yes.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:57.420
If the Diva crew were weaklings, who were wasting the AGE System,

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:02.340
I was going to take it for ourselves and make better use of it.

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:05.510
But they weren't weaklings.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:10.430
That ship, and Flit Asuno, are as strong as ever.

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:12.600
I can leave the AGE System to them.

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:14.680
And one more thing...

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.640
The Gundam pilot?

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:18.900
Yes. I've entrusted it to him.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:24.570
The key to the treasure that will determine the course of the war.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.950
Now, what will he do with it?

